 :what-went-wrong-in-the-measurement
 "Five warmup iterations is not enough for a JIT-compiled three-clause join, and
  one start person makes the sample a property of that person's degree. The
  earlier probe also measured BEFORE first in both passes, so the arm that ran
  second always had a warmer machine -- which flatters AFTER on scans and,
  because the JVMs were separate, does nothing for it on IC02.

  The failure mode is worth naming: the previous receipt was CAUTIOUS in the
  right direction -- it withheld a change on evidence of harm -- and the caution
  was built on a measurement too weak to support either conclusion. Refusing to
  land on bad evidence is not safer than landing on it; both are unmeasured."

 :the-running-tally
 "Five hypotheses about IC02's per-row cost, all measured: quad map 6%,
  intermediate set 0.15%, `map vector` in unify 26% of the sub-term. Of those,
  one was worth landing and it is worth about 2-5% on IC02. IC02 remains ~9.7x
  Neo4j on the paired ratio; nothing found so far explains that gap."}
